 impact on their lives they are trying to  appeal to the bond that they share with  deku as  his friends and his classmates but  no matter what the other students say or  do deku refuses to stay down  he tells his classmates that all for one  is coming after him  and he has to leave for that very reason  if he doesn't leave he will put everyone  close to him  in imminent danger and so deku keeps  struggling  he keeps breaking out of every makeshift  restraint that the other students create  and he keeps pushing forward tokuyam  even attempts to wrap deku  inside a dark shadow generated cocoon a  move that tokoyami says was inspired by  deku himself but even that is not enough  to restrain  our incredibly stubborn protagonist he  manages to break free yet again  and he tells his classmates that he's  fine even though he clearly doesn't  look fine after he escapes from dark  shadows cocoon  deku's mask symbolically flies off  revealing his tortured  facial expression to some extent deku  was trying to hide  behind that mask it was easier for him  to turn away from his friends while the  mask was  protecting him the mask was hiding his  facial expression  from his friends and it allowed him to  maintain his new  lone wolf vigilante persona but when the  mask flies off  everything inevitably becomes a lot more  real and a lot more  personal for daku daku begs his  classmates to get away from him and just  let him leave  but before he can escape he runs into a  wall of ice  created by todoroki todoroki tells deku  that he must let them share his burden  he can't keep trying to carry the weight  of the entire world on his  own shoulders and this is what i've been  talking about for a while now  all of deku's class 1a classmates are  also working hard to become heroes he's  not the only one  and heroes are prepared to take risks in  order to do good and  save innocent people yes it is risky to  stay with deku while he is being  targeted by villains  but his classmates are 